<%# Reviewer decision card (civora-org/civora-platform#90), shared by the
    two admin surfaces so their markup stays in sync — the reason core
    lives in _review_decision_body. Read-only on both: the decision is
    reviewer-typed historical record, neither surface offers a control to
    change it (the editor's answer is the resubmit transition).
    Locals:
      contract - the record whose decision to show
      collapsed - false (default): the edit page's full banner — the
                  editor's answer to "why was this returned?"; renders
                  regardless of role (historical record) whenever the
                  caller's reason/state gate admits it.
                  true: the admin index row's collapsed read-only
                  <details> — only the short summary label shows until
                  opened. The index caller gates on reason presence only:
                  any admin who can see the row may read it (the same
                  audience as the index) — deliberately no permission
                  check, unlike the redaction card, since reading a past
                  decision is not a write. For a rejected record that row
                  card is the only reachable surface for its reason: a
                  terminal state renders no transition controls and the
                  edit page stays permission-locked. %>
<% collapsed = local_assigns.fetch(:collapsed, false) %>
<% if collapsed %>
  <details class="review-decision-reason">
    <summary><%= t("decidim.contracts_sk.admin.contracts.review_decision.heading") %></summary>
    <%= render "review_decision_body", contract: contract %>
  </details>
<% else %>
  <div class="card review-decision-banner">
    <div class="card-divider">
      <h2 class="card-title">
        <%= t("decidim.contracts_sk.admin.contracts.review_decision.heading") %>
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="card-section">
      <%= render "review_decision_body", contract: contract %>
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>
